BLOCK 1: STARTER ({starterMinutes} minutes)
ONE open task the whole class can start on at once, leading into today's goals. It must:
- fit on one slide or the board; write it out verbatim;
- be OPEN: many answers or routes, so students can keep going for several minutes;
- have a low threshold: a student who knows none of today's material can start. Build on nothing beyond the prerequisite list below, preferably less. This is the hardest requirement;
- invite trying, guessing, comparing with a neighbour and adjusting.
Add 2–3 sentences to the teacher on how it leads into the goals and what to look for while the students work.
